    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our elite 81.88 efficiency score. His matchup against Arrighetti is exceptionally favorable; beyond the strong ATC projection, the slow delivery of the opposing starter creates an environment where **Gunnar Henderson** has a distinct tactical advantage to exploit our league\u2019s premium on stolen bases. Joining him at the top of the board is **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), who benefits from a generous 4.99 xERA matchup against Dobnak. The combination of **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s batting order placement and the 19% SP skill boost makes him a near-automatic start. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) are standout plays, with both capitalizing on significant SP skill bumps and park-factor elevations that push them well into the \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished with a 58.79 score. While **Nasim Nunez** was an enticing candidate for his speed profile, his projected slot in the #9 hole\u2014resulting in an 8% penalty\u2014ultimately tipped the optimizer toward playing the more efficient **Curtis Mead** (62.15). Elsewhere, we are leaning into favorable platoon dynamics; **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.06) both benefit from elite xwOBA metrics and favorable SP matchups, allowing them to provide solid middle-order stability. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.98) rounds out our core, holding steady despite a slight platoon penalty.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Curtis Mead**. Should any of these players move down in the order or be held out, their efficiency scores will crater, forcing a pivot to bench options like **Josh Jung** or **Brayan Rocchio**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Drake Baldwin**, whose 58.04 score is highly dependent on his #1 spot; if that top-of-the-order protection shifts, he risks falling toward our \"Below Floor\" threshold. Aside from these situational risks, the lineup is well-positioned to capitalize on a day of soft opposing pitching.",
